   550	\section{ Non-divisible Sum Graphs} 
   551	In Figure 10, we have given some non-divisible sum  graphs $G_m,_n$  for given values of $m$ and $n$  which are additively graceful.  The labels of the vertices are from the set $\{0, 1, ...,\left\lceil\frac{q+1}{2}\right\rceil\}$, $q$ is in $G_m,_n$.
   552	We observe that these graphs are complement reducible.
